. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>533</fpage>&#x02013;541.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8461140</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Clay, J.R. <year>1995</year>. Quaternary ammonium ion blockade of I<sub>K</sub> in nerve axons revisited. Open channel block vs. state independent block. <source>J. Membr. Biol.</source> <volume>147</volume>:<fpage>23</fpage>&#x02013;34.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8531197</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Colquhoun, D., F. Dreyer, and R.E. Sheridan. <year>1979</year>. The actions of tubocurarine at the frog neuromuscular junction. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>293</volume>:<fpage>247</fpage>&#x02013;284.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">315462</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Cox, D.H., J. Cui, and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1997</year>. Separation of gating properties from permeation and block in <italic>mslo</italic> large conductance Ca-activated K<sup>+</sup> channels. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>109</volume>:<fpage>633</fpage>&#x02013;646.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9154909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Cui, J., D.H. Cox, and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1997</year>. Intrinsic voltage dependence and Ca<sup>2+</sup> regulation of <italic>mslo</italic> large conductance Ca-activated K<sup>+</sup> channels. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>109</volume>:<fpage>647</fpage>&#x02013;673.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9154910</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Diaz, F., M. Wallner, E. Stefani, L. Toro, and R. Latorre. <year>1996</year>. Interaction of internal Ba<sup>2+</sup> with a cloned Ca<sup>2+</sup>-dependent K<sup>+</sup> (<italic>hslo</italic>) channel from smooth muscle. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>107</volume>:<fpage>399</fpage>&#x02013;407.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8868050</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Ding, S., and R. Horn. <year>2002</year>. Tail end of the s6 segment: role in permeation in shaker potassium channels. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>87</fpage>&#x02013;97.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12084778</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Doyle, D.A., J. Morais Cabral, R.A. Pfuetzner, A. Kuo, J.M. Gulbis, S.L. Cohen, B.T. Chait, and R. MacKinnon. <year>1998</year>. The structure of the potassium channel: molecular basis of K<sup>+</sup> conduction and selectivity. <source>Science.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>69</fpage>&#x02013;77.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9525859</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Foster, C.D., S. Chung, W.N. Zagotta, R.W. Aldrich, and I.B. Levitan. <year>1992</year>. A peptide derived from the Shaker B K<sup>+</sup> channel produces short and long blocks of reconstituted Ca<sup>2+</sup>-dependent K<sup>+</sup> channels. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>229</fpage>&#x02013;236.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1497892</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">French, R.J., and J.J. Shoukimas. <year>1981</year>. Blockage of squid axon potassium conductance by internal tetra-N-alkylammonium ions of various sizes. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>34</volume>:<fpage>271</fpage>&#x02013;291.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7236852</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Guo, D., and Z. Lu. <year>2001</year>. Kinetics of inward-rectifier K<sup>+</sup> channel block by quaternary alkylammonium ions. dimension and properties of the inner pore. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>117</volume>:<fpage>395</fpage>&#x02013;406.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11331349</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Hamill, O.P., A. Marty, E. Neher, B. Sakmann, and F.J. Sigworth. <yea